#   LAN to Internet - internet.https: the source of the rule is in zone eth1, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind eth1 with --zone-network; the destination of the rule is in zone WAN, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind WAN with --zone-network
#   LAN to Internet - standard.dns: the source of the rule is in zone eth1, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind eth1 with --zone-network; the destination of the rule is in zone WAN, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind WAN with --zone-network
#   LAN to Internet - standard.ping: the source of the rule is in zone eth1, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind eth1 with --zone-network; the destination of the rule is in zone WAN, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind WAN with --zone-network
#   Internet to Webserver - internet.https: the source of the rule is in zone WAN, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind WAN with --zone-network; the destination of the rule is in zone eth2, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind eth2 with --zone-network
#   Admin-PCs to Servers - standard.ssh: the source of the rule is in zone eth1, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind eth1 with --zone-network; the destination of the rule is in zone eth2, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind eth2 with --zone-network
#   Admin-PCs to Servers - remote.rdp: the source of the rule is in zone eth1, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind eth1 with --zone-network; the destination of the rule is in zone eth2, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind eth2 with --zone-network
#   Servers to Admin-PCs - remote.rdp: the source of the rule is in zone eth2, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind eth2 with --zone-network; the destination of the rule is in zone eth1, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind eth1 with --zone-network
#   Jump-Hosts to OT-Cell - Modbus-TCP (eth1 to eth3): the source of the rule is in zone eth1, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind eth1 with --zone-network; the destination of the rule is in zone eth3, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind eth3 with --zone-network
