#   LAN to DMZ - Web: the source of the rule is in zone eth1, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind eth1 with --zone-network; the destination of the rule is in zone eth2, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind eth2 with --zone-network
#   DMZ to LAN - Web: the source of the rule is in zone eth2, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind eth2 with --zone-network; the destination of the rule is in zone eth1, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind eth1 with --zone-network
#   DMZ to LAN - vpn.ipsec: the source of the rule is in zone eth2, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind eth2 with --zone-network; the destination of the rule is in zone eth1, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind eth1 with --zone-network
#   Printer to DMZ - internet.http: not converted: desktop object 'Printer' cannot be read: a host that names no interface; the destination of the rule is in zone eth2, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind eth2 with --zone-network

echo 'Done. Associate the policy with the network when you are ready; until then nothing changes.' >&2
